=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[First aid provides immediate assistance and does not replace clinical care. First aid is immediate assistance, not a complete clinical treatment.]

#sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[First aid aims to support life, prevent further harm and provide reassurance. Reassurance and prevention of further harm are also important aims.]

#sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Scene safety helps prevent the rescuer becoming another casualty. Traffic, electricity or fire can create hazards for the rescuer.]

#sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Do not touch someone in contact with a live source; arrange safe disconnection and call for help. A person in contact with live electricity must not be touched until it is safe.]

#sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Do not enter an unsafe area and become another casualty. Emergency services can coordinate help without exposing another person to danger.]

#sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Accurate location and scene information help emergency responders. Give a precise location and explain hazards where possible.]

#sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Dispatcher guidance and appropriate training are important in an emergency. Guidance and training help match the response to the situation.]

#sol-item(8, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Obtain consent where appropriate and follow applicable local procedures. Communication matters when a person is able to respond.]

#sol-item(9, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Appropriate protective equipment can reduce exposure but does not eliminate all risk. Appropriate protective equipment complements scene safety.]

#sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Unresponsiveness and abnormal breathing require urgent help and CPR guidance. Do not delay calling while trying to make a diagnosis.]

#sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[An automated external defibrillator analyses rhythm and provides instructions. The device provides prompts to guide its use.]

#sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Follow AED prompts and emergency dispatcher guidance. Follow the device and dispatcher instructions while help is arranged.]

#sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[CPR techniques can vary; training and local guidance matter. Age and situation may affect appropriate CPR procedures.]

#sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Monitor breathing, call for help and follow dispatcher guidance. Breathing may change, so continued monitoring matters.]

#sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A recovery position can help when an unresponsive person breathes normally, subject to circumstances and guidance. Recovery position is not a substitute for CPR when normal breathing is absent.]

#sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Avoid unnecessary movement unless needed for safety or essential care; follow emergency guidance.]

#sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Forcing anything into the mouth of an unresponsive person can be dangerous.]

#sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Call for help and apply appropriate direct pressure to severe bleeding.]

#sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Removing an embedded object can worsen bleeding; pressure is applied around it.]

#sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A tourniquet can be appropriate for life-threatening limb bleeding when used according to training.]

#sol-item(21, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Firm pressure can help control severe bleeding while emergency care is arranged.]

#sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cool running water is recommended for thermal burns; avoid ice or unverified substances.]

#sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[NHS guidance recommends cooling a thermal burn under cool running water for 20 minutes where possible.]

#sol-item(24, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cool the burn while keeping the rest of the person warm.]

#sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Do not pull away material stuck to burned skin.]

#sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Serious burns need urgent assessment and guidance suited to the cause.]

#sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Keep the injured area still and obtain appropriate assessment.]

#sol-item(28, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Do not push a protruding bone back; seek appropriate emergency care.]

#sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Avoid unnecessary movement unless required for safety or essential care.]

#sol-item(30, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Protect the responder while arranging urgent help and following guidance.]

#sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Secure, labelled storage is one part of prevention.]

#sol-item(32, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Misleading containers can lead to accidental exposure.]

#sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A kit supports trained response but is not a substitute for care.]

#sol-item(34, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A practical plan defines responsibilities, location, equipment and access needs.]

#sol-item(35, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Emergency arrangements differ; verify the appropriate number locally.]

#sol-item(36, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Breathing can change and the dispatcher should be updated.]

#sol-item(37, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Different conditions require different responses and guidance.]

#sol-item(38, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Reassurance and monitoring can support care while help is arranged.]

#sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[First aid depends on the injury and circumstances.]

#sol-item(40, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Practical training and local emergency instructions are essential.]
